// Title: Dropping Of Password Filter DLL
// Sigma ID: b7966f4a-b333-455b-8370-8ca53c229762
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sreeman
// Date: 2020-10-29 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: persistence, credential-access, defense-impairment, T1556.002
// Description: Detects dropping of dll files in system32 that may be used to retrieve user credentials from
//   LSASS
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2020/02/10/credential-access-password-filter-dll/
//   - https://github.com/3gstudent/PasswordFilter/tree/master/PasswordFilter
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_credential_access_via_password_filter.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa" and ProcessCommandLine contains "scecli\\0" and ProcessCommandLine contains "reg add"
